full_article:
Since leaving Covington more than two decades ago, Ralph "Beau" Menetre has been on the go.

The businessman helped create a small film festival near his adopted hometown in North Carolina called the Tryon International Film Festival, or TRIFF, and has built it into one of the most respected of its kind.

“Our whole town is about 1,600 people, and we get 1,000 people in for the film festival,” Menetre said recently while in New Orleans for a conference. “Don’t ask me what we do about housing everyone who comes. We get real creative.”

